
################
# Demo version #
################

DESC 1 Empty Room
This room is about as full as a can of beer in a room full of alcoholics.
The bland colour walls are bare, and a thin film of dust has settled on the
floor.  There is really nothing interesting about this room at all.
ENDDESC

DESC 2 North-South Hallway
This hallway extends to the north and south.
ENDDESC

DESC 3 East-West Hallway
This hallway extends to the east and west.
ENDDESC

DESC 4 North-West Corner
This hallway extends to the south and east.
ENDDESC

DESC 5 North-East Corner
This hallway extends to the south and west.
ENDDESC

DESC 6 South-West Corner
This hallway extends to the north and east.
ENDDESC

DESC 7 South-East Corner
This hallway extends to the north and west.
ENDDESC

DESC 8 End of Hallway
This hallway has come to an abrupt halt.
ENDDESC

DESC 9 Hallway Intersection
You are at an intersection of hallways, a point in your life in which you
must make a decision of which path to take.  The choice you make here may
have significant outcomes in the near far or really distant future.  But
then again, maybe it won't.
ENDDESC

DESC 10 Auto-Medical Room
This room provides medical services to those agents who wish to heal or
improve their skills.  An automated nurse idles in anticipation to prepare
you for the automated doctor.  An audio/video component in this room has
its screen-saver enabled while it awaits for an agent to insert some credits
to activate one of its skills videos.
ENDDESC

DESC 11 Sleeping Room
Along the walls of this room are cell cavities where agents may sleep in
a safe and secure fashion.  If you exit from this virtual imagination game
in this room, you are stored in one of these cavities until you become
conscious again.  This service is provided compliments of Cells-R-Us Inc.
ENDDESC

DESC 12 Recycling Room
There are holes lining the floor and walls of this room, each with its
own unique name label.  You can recycle your unwanted and used equipment
here for some credits in return.  We like to promote an environmentally
friendly underground self-supporting complex.
ENDDESC

DESC 13 Toys for Big Kids
There are large vending machines built into the walls of this room, each
able to dispense its very own unique destructive little weapon or armour.
For just a few couple many alot whole-bunch of credits, you can purchase
that toy that Santa could never bring you.  There is a disclaimer note
on the wall that states, 'No one accepts responsibility should one of
these mother mammoth little big vending machines not work or blow up'.
ENDDESC

DESC 14 Control Room
This area is the control room, where all the powers that be can control
what goes on within the complex.  But the desertion of the terminals give
you a feeling that this place is no longer active and is more representative
of a museum than a control area.
ENDDESC

DESC 15 Vertical Shaft
This shaft extends up and down.
ENDDESC

DESC 16 End of Shaft
This shaft has come to an abrupt halt.
ENDDESC

DESC 17 Hallway Alcove
This little area is just off the side of the hallway and has an arch above.
ENDDESC

DESC 18 Storage Room
This storage area is where non-perishable food, tools, and miscellaneous
weapons of destruction are stored.
ENDDESC

DESC 19 Storage Room
This storage area is where non-perishable food, tools, and miscellaneous
weapons of destruction are stored.
ENDDESC

DESC 20 Interrogation Room
This part of the complex reminds you of a bad dream you once had.  A large
open area with a couple chairs, a couple spotlights, and no opportunity of
waking up.  This is one dream you don't want to come true.
ENDDESC

DESC 21 Access Corridor
This corridor is used for quick access between the Control Room and the
Interrogation Room.  It was designed after one of the complex co-ordinators
was crippled from an accidental fall into the Pit.
ENDDESC

DESC 22 Holding Cell
This cell is furnished with its very own cot, sink, and toilet.  Among the
essentials, it also comes with a vent for climate control and plenty of wall
space for pictures and posters.  This room lacks windows... and privacy.
ENDDESC

DESC 23 Access Corridor
This corridor is used for quick access through the Empty Room Complex.
It was designed after one of the complex co-ordinators lost his way and
eventually died of starvation.
ENDDESC

